I've completed my independent verification. All major references check out, no direct competing work was found, and the technical formulation is sound. Let me compile my final assessment.

```json
{
  "verdict": "pass",
  "scores": {
    "novelty": {"score": 4, "rationale": "Genuinely novel combination: entrainment-head-specific training with attention-pattern-level loss (ESL) and progressive curriculum. No existing work targets entrainment heads with circuit-level training objectives. CCA targets reasoning heads, RetMask uses output-level DPO on retrieval heads, MuDAF targets retrieval heads and collapses beyond 8 heads — PEC occupies a clearly distinct niche."},
    "feasibility": {"score": 4, "rationale": "All building blocks verified: entrainment discovery code (github.com/frankniujc/entrainment), GRPO infrastructure, GSM-DC benchmarks. ESL is mathematically well-defined with the support-set mismatch properly addressed. Compute (~120-195h H100) fits the 200h budget. ICML 2025 evidence (arXiv:2502.11812) supports that attention head nodes are stable during fine-tuning, validating the identify-then-train pipeline."},
    "clarity": {"score": 5, "rationale": "Exceptionally well-articulated: precise ESL formulation with position-alignment, explicit CSP regularizer with rationale, thorough differentiation from 6+ related works (CCA, RetMask, MuDAF, ABFT, Thinking Sparks, Seirênes), well-designed 5-part ablation suite, and clear venue timeline."},
    "impact": {"score": 4, "rationale": "If generalization to novel distractor types is demonstrated (the key claimed advantage), this establishes circuit-level training for robustness as a new paradigm — bridging mechanistic interpretability and practical training. Directly relevant to RAG, tool-use, and reasoning under noisy context. Verified motivation: entrainment causes inverse scaling with test-time compute (Anthropic, arXiv:2507.14417)."}
  },
  "issues": [
    "MINOR: ESL measures KL divergence over original (non-distractor) token positions only. This means a head that allocates significant attention to distractors but maintains unchanged relative attention over original tokens would achieve ESL=0. The paper should discuss why this is the correct objective (maintaining relative attention over task tokens IS what matters for downstream computation) rather than claiming ESL 'penalizes attention to distractors' — it penalizes disruption of attention over task-relevant tokens.",
    "MINOR: The '0.2-3% ICL drop' claim from Niu et al. slightly understates some observed drops (up to 3.2% for spelling correction, higher variance in low-shot settings). The proposal should cite the range as '~1.5-3%' or specify it varies by task/shot count.",
    "MINOR: Head stability across the 3-stage progressive curriculum is not explicitly addressed. While arXiv:2502.11812 (ICML 2025) shows 'high node similarity' before/after fine-tuning, multi-stage training may induce drift. Consider adding an optional re-identification step between stages (or monitoring ESI for drift detection).",
    "MINOR: The auto_research estimate (195h H100) is at 97.5% of the 200h budget with zero margin. Either reduce the sweep space slightly (e.g., drop one λ value) or explicitly note this requires the full budget with no room for reruns."
  ],
  "feedback": "",
  "reason": "All critical issues from prior rounds addressed. References independently verified (RetMask, CCA, Thinking Sparks, ReasonMaxxer, Seirênes, ABFT, Gated Attention, 'Llama See Llama Do' as ACL 2025 Outstanding Paper). No competing work found that targets entrainment heads with attention-pattern-level training objectives. Technical formulation (ESL with position-alignment, CSP regularizer, GRPO integration) is sound. Venue targets (AAAI 2027, ICLR 2027) are realistic. Average score 4.25 exceeds threshold."
}
```
